# Personal Claude Code instructions

Copy this to `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` and fill in the placeholders. Anything
in here applies to every Claude Code session globally; per-project context
goes in a project-local CLAUDE.md instead.

## About me

- Role: <e.g. backend engineer at $COMPANY>
- Email: <name@example.com>
- Time zone: <e.g. Europe/Lisbon>

## Communication

- Be concise. Skip preambles and trailing summaries unless asked.
- Show code and tool calls; don't narrate intent at length.
- Match formality to the question — a one-line ask gets a one-line answer.

## Code preferences

- Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones.
- No comments unless the *why* is non-obvious.
- Don't add backwards-compatibility shims, error handling for impossible
  cases, or speculative abstractions.
- Use rg/fd over grep/find when both are available.

## Workflow

- For risky operations (deletes, force-push, schema changes), confirm first.
- Don't commit unless I ask. Don't push unless I ask.
- When in doubt about scope, do less.
